  <section data-figma-id="351:162" class="d-ceca30ddf">
    <p data-figma-id="351:163" class="d-e7e8576a1">
      SAMENSTAD
    </p>
    <div data-figma-id="351:164" class="d-72320dbab">
      <div data-figma-id="351:165" class="d-3c11b8280">
        <p data-figma-id="351:166" class="d-0983a75de">
          UX case study · Civic technology · 's-Hertogenbosch, NL
        </p>
        <h1 data-figma-id="351:167" class="d-56c06a713">
          <span class="d-676876d08">Samen</span>
          <span class="d-40f7d1224">stad</span>
        </h1>
        <p data-figma-id="351:168" class="d-0bdd719e1">
          samen (together) + stad (city) — &quot;your city, fixed together&quot;
        </p>
        <p data-figma-id="351:169" class="d-f85dfc262">
          Every city reporting app opens with the same question: what is broken? Samenstad opens
          with a different one — where are you standing? That single reversal turns six neighbours
          filing six identical complaints into one issue a municipality can actually act on, and
          gives the street a way to fix what the budget cannot.
        </p>
      </div>
